cdi wrote:
> corvine@gmail.com wrote:
> > I searched for a while, gave up, got a wish from my
> > magic lamp and wished for the Eye for MR. Sokoban had the amulet of
> > reflec
> > Jayne the Student of Stones     St:18/20 Dx:17 Co:17 In:10 Wi:13 Ch:9
> > Neutral
> > Dlvl:27 $:2158 HP:108(108) Pw:48(71) AC:-4 Exp:13

That AC is your biggest problem.

You should easily be able to find a better replacement for:

> >  m - a rusty +0 helmet (being worn)

by BUC testing items in the dungeon and putting them on.  Elvish
leather helms are ideal and usually by the castle you've found at least
a +1 or +2 one.  If not then sacrificing a bit of casting for a
dwarvish helm is maybe worth it.

You should also have found a decent small shield by now.  Wear it, it
only takes one turn to take it off for casting.

> >  E - a +0 cloak of invisibility

> >  N - a +0 pair of boots called jumping boots

Wear these.  The +0 elven aren't buying you anything since you have
intrinsic stealth.  Jumping is a way out of a lot of jams.

And you want to enchant up all of the above.

> >  Wands
> >  d - a wand of teleportation (0:8)

Do not hesitate to use this to get out of trouble--and remember that
it's often best to zap it at a tough foe rather than at yourself.  The
former works on no-teleport levels (like the Castle) too, the latter
may be better if you're surrounded.

> >  l - a wand of enlightenment (0:10)

As a monk, you're going to get the Eyes which can be invoked for
enlightenment.  So use this liberally whenever you need to see if a
ring/amulet/etc does anything or if you just need to double-check
intrinsics/prayer timeout.

> >  k - a magic marker (0:40)

Write blessed ?enchant armor (assuming you've found at least one of
those already), bless the ?charging and use it when you get too low on
charges, and write more blessed ?enchant armor.

You'll wish up another marker to write another ?charging at the Castle
(for the wand).  Getting AC down now is valuable.

> >  Y - an uncursed magic whistle

Not even a sack?  Sacks protect potions/scrolls/rings/spellbooks/etc
that are inside them from environmental damage.  And make it so you can
carry more items.

> > I don't have levitation/water walking and my wand of cold is empty. I
> > think I need to go back up into the dungeons and improve my AC somehow
Yes.

> > (maybe explore a couple of levels more fully and try and find an altar)
> > but I don't know how I can get back to the upstairs on Medusa save
> > using the scroll of charging on my wand of cold or invoking the Eye
> > (but that takes you to the lowest level you've explored, right? so
> > mine's end?)

As was noted, jumping can always cross medusa.  Also, the Eye is
fine--it'll ask you what branch (Dungeons of Doom, Sokoban, Mines, etc)
you want and take you to the lowest level of that.  Bottom level of
Sokoban is generally a fine destination, and it's worth setting your
main base camp up there simply because you can get to it easily with
the Eye.

> > in attack and enchantment spells, Skilled in healing, I have Healing,
> > Charm Monster and Magic Missile at 0% fail amongst others.

Charm monster is awesome.

> > I keep running out of inventory
> > letters

A sack will help with that.  There's one in perseus.  /striking, force
bolt, or pickaxe/mattock to get in--you can surely get a pick from the
mines to use.

> > Secondarily - I've investigated the Quest home level a little. Got
> > surrounded by X and E, bottled it and ran. That's been my only
> > almost-death so far. I hear Master Kaen is a bit nasty and I should
> > just NOT EVEN GO THERE yet...

There are ways to make him a pushover, but I'd wait if I were you.

> Don't stress out over your AC, you have the tools to improve it.  When
> you come across useless scrolls, blank them and use your marker.

Stress over it a little, as in it's worth going back and doing the
marker/scroll thing right now.  But yes you have the tools to address
it.

> Watch out for minotaurs.  They don't respect the e-word and hit
> *really* hard.  I'm no expert on the best way to deal with them, so
> I'll defer to others' advice on that.

Sleep works.

> Have a plan for the castle wand before you get it.  ID the wand charges
> *before* you use it, and only use a blessed ?charging on it.  You will
> have at least 5 wishes, I'd use them on the following (blessed and
> foo-proofed):

You don't want to use them all when you get the wand unless there are
things you need to survive.

Having a couple wishes in the sack is a _huge_ advantage, in case you
forget something for the end game or whatever.

You don't want to die with wishes in the sack that could've saved you,
but if waiting until later (and getting, say, a cockatrice corpse for
Astral) will increase your survival odds then do that.

> 1) magic marker

yes, at least one.  AC is key, and getting magic mapping for gehennom
and gold detection for planes is good too.
And of course ?charging for the wand if you've used the one you have
already (Blessed!  blessed!)
> 2) PYEC <- only if you can safely wish for it.

Ehh, only uncursed charging for non-tourists.  With the Eye for MR
already, not all _that_ useful.

> 3) bag of holding

Luxury item that I would go for.  blessed greased bag of holding, of
course.

> 4) +3 Hawaiian Shirt <- check the castle store rooms first

Depends on his AC.  Even with bad rolls on the enchantment front, he
could easily have 10 protection, +6 elvish helm, +4 robe, +4 jumping
boots, +4 gloves for -23 AC by then with a +4 small shield to get -28
while not casting.  I'd rather wish for a /polymorph to polypile or
wait through most of Gehennom before using a wish on a shirt.

Definitely check the store rooms before this and before any artifact
wishes, sometimes artifact weapons are in the weapon room!

> 5) spellbook of remove curse, if you don't know know it already.

By now (or very shortly) this is a pretty useless spell, you'll be
swimming in holy water once you get the bag of holding and go back
through the dungeons and grab all the ones you left behind on the way
down.

This spellbook is one of the most worthless in the game, IMO; for most
classes, by the time you can cast it even somewhat successfully it's no
longer useful.  If you start off with some talent in it then it can be
kind of useful early on, so it's not quite as bad as restore ability or
a couple others.

> Get the castle wand before undertaking the quest.  If you've seen a
> musical instrument, go back and get it ... it'll make the castle much
> easier.

Definitely.

> Kaen can be turned into a pushover.  He hits *really* hard, the trick
> is, don't let him hit you.  Boulder fort, levitate over lava, whatever
> ... deal with him from a distance.

Yes.  But I'd wait a bit longer as a new player so that you have some
margin for error.  The first several levels of Gehennom down to
Orcustown will be pretty safe if you get that AC down and play smart.

> You've got a good game going, good luck!

Yes, good luck!



